### SDDK ledger projection (regenerable, not repository authority) ###
# BACKLOG.md is a rendered projection of an SDDK project ledger. It is NOT
# project documentation: the copy present here was rendered from a different
# SDDK project id (p-733fb505b5a6bd2d), not this repository (p-1f3622e11c093341).
# Standing constraint: .agent/HANDOFF-S1-TRAIN-20260929.md ("do not
# commit/delete"). Ignored rather than deleted so the file stays on disk.
BACKLOG.md

# Runtime-only E2E/UAT/AAT cycles: no scripts, fixtures or evidence checked in
/.verification-cycles/
/.verification-results/

# No build or evidence output under examples
/examples/**/.pipelinek/
/examples/**/build/
/examples/**/*.db
/examples/**/*.sqlite*
/examples/**/*.log
/examples/**/*.jsonl

### Mission declaration (local configuration) ###
# The goal chain's declaration and its working directory are local configuration
# of this checkout, not repository content: a tool that leaves unversioned files
# in someone else's repository earns their mistrust. This only says where the
# chain starts.
/.goal-compass/
goal-compass.json

### Work records (local, not repository content) ###
# The roadmap file that used to live here is GONE (2026-11-03): it was a second
# copy of the state of the work that the task manager already holds, and a
# second copy that can disagree with the code is the drift this repository
# keeps paying for. The context of the open work is in the task manager
# (backlog/), and the history of what was already done is in Git. The rule
# stays so that a stray copy of that file does not come back into the index.
# The uppercase BACKLOG.md above is a DIFFERENT file: an old SDDK projection,
# kept on disk and ignored.
/ROADMAP.md
/backlog/
# The importer that moved the 2026-11 audit plan into the board. It is a
# management tool, not product: it carries the task texts that already live
# in Backlog.md, and a second copy of them in Git is the drift this
# repository keeps paying for.
/backlog-import-auditoria-2026-11.sh

.codegraph/

